📅 Day 35 – Introduction to CSS

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session introduced CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) and its role in enhancing the design and presentation of web pages. The mentor explained how CSS is used to style HTML elements and improve the visual appearance of websites.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to CSS

CSS is used to style and format HTML elements.

It controls layout, colors, fonts, spacing, and overall design.

Helps separate content (HTML) from presentation (CSS).

2️⃣ Types of CSS

The mentor explained three ways to apply CSS:

✅ Inline CSS

Applied directly inside HTML tags

Example: <p style="color:red;">Text</p>

✅ Internal CSS

Defined inside <style> tag within <head> section

✅ External CSS

Written in a separate .css file

Linked using <link> tag

Best practice for large projects

3️⃣ Basic CSS Concepts

Selectors → Target HTML elements

Color → color, background-color

Font Styling → font-size, font-family

Spacing → margin, padding

Borders → border, border-radius

